  "name": "Lakhon bassac (Khmer popular opera)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Popular theatre created by Khmer people near the Bassac river in the Mekong Delta of southern Vietnam at the beginning of the twentieth century, and taken up by troupes in Phnom Penh and across Cambodia. Drawing on Chinese opera, it combines costume, face painting, acrobatics and fight scenes with sung dialogue, and its orchestra joins the tro fiddle and other melodic instruments with drums, gongs, chimes and wood blocks. Generic drum, gong and auxiliary-percussion cards stand in for the percussion section.",
